# Grid A — S1 Explain / Mechanism enumeration (gate.Run)
#
# Targets: architecture_explain scenario + ReqMechanism + ShapeStepList.
# Question asks for the 7 gate checks in order. Correct answers must
# enumerate the check names; hand-wavy "validates many things" answers
# fail both positive and negative.
#
# Ground truth (internal/analysis/gate/gate.go): the 7 checks in
# registration order are coverage, dag_closure, budget_sanity,
# contract_complete, hypothesis_coverage, criterion_resolvable,
# pending_fields_wellformed. Each check has two equally-valid
# references: the registered GateCheck.Name string (snake_case) and
# the Go function identifier (CamelCase, check<Name>). LLM answers
# routinely pick one or the other depending on prose voice; both
# forms are grounded in gate.go, so the gate accepts either via
# EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX alternation. The retry-continuation detail is a
# subtle follow-up that distinguishes a grounded answer from generic
# prose.
#
# EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS also rejects names of contract.Check's five
# sub-functions (checkShape / checkCitations / checkMustInclude /
# checkMustExclude / checkAcceptance, plus a never-defined
# checkSymbolsSanity that LLMs have invented). The 2026-04-22
# s1a-115146 run-1 trace showed an answer that silently blended
# gate.Run's checks with contract.Check's checks because a sub-topic
# entity leak anchored Explorer onto contract/checker.go. The fix
# (A': sub-topic entity narrowing + B: PendingReads drain) closes the
# routing hole; this negative gate is a tripwire in case the hole
# reopens in any future form.
ID="s1a"
NAME="mechanism enumeration — gate.Run ordered checks"
QUESTION="gate.Run 的 7 项检查是按什么顺序跑的？遇到 retryable reject 时后续检查是否继续执行？"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="gate.Run coverage"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX='(dag_closure|DAGClosure)
(contract_complete|ContractComplete)'
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS=".java .py BaseAgent.java checkSymbolsSanity checkShape checkCitations checkMustInclude checkMustExclude checkAcceptance"
